            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 15:2",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "And he walked in all the sins of his father, which he had done before him: and his heart was not perfect with the Lord his God, as the heart of David his father.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 128,
            "end": 130,
            "text": "JST 1 Kgs. 15:3 … as the Lord commanded David his father."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 15:3",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "Nevertheless for David’s sake did the Lord his God give him a lamp in Jerusalem, to set up his son after him, and to establish Jerusalem:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 15:4",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "Because David did that which was right in the eyes of the Lord, and turned not aside from any thing that he commanded him all the days of his life, save only in the matter of Uriah the Hittite.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 13,
            "text": "1 Kgs. 9:4."
          },
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 74,
            "text": "Deut. 17:20."
          },
          {
            "start": 175,
            "end": 180,
            "text": "2 Sam. 11:3 (3–15); 1 Kgs. 14:8; D&C 132:39."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 32
          },
          {
            "start": 94,
            "end": 99
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
